00:44:26.630 --> 00:44:29.880
And yet, they both have very similar.

00:44:30.280 --> 00:44:38.340
body shapes. They're a remarkable example of what's called convergent evolution, two groups

00:44:38.340 --> 00:44:47.170
of unrelated animals that have evolved similar bodies to suit the same environment. But there

00:44:47.170 --> 00:44:55.060
are some differences. Dolphins beat their tails up and down like their cousins, the whales.

00:44:56.930 --> 00:44:59.970
Aethiosaurs, as is clear from their fossils, had...

00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:02.980
Tails like fish that beat from side to side.

00:45:03.420 --> 00:45:09.230
And dolphins only have two flippers, whereas ichthyosaurs had four.

00:45:11.800 --> 00:45:18.240
So, is it possible that ichthyosaurs were as fast in the water and as agile as dolphins?

