00:49:08.890 --> 00:49:15.410
They were the hips and back legs of some kind of giant reptile.

00:49:18.040 --> 00:49:19.260
More of them were discovered,

00:49:19.420 --> 00:49:23.340
and soon they were enough to get some idea of what the whole animal had looked like.

00:49:26.500 --> 00:49:29.600
One odd little bone seemed to have nowhere to go.

00:49:30.030 --> 00:49:32.870
So the reconstructors put it on the end of its nose,

00:49:33.220 --> 00:49:36.760
making the animal look like some kind of reptilian rhinoceros.

00:49:39.260 --> 00:49:42.320
It was like nothing anyone had ever seen before.

00:49:45.500 --> 00:49:50.490
So, a great fossil hunt started in the quarries of Sussex,

00:49:51.120 --> 00:49:56.290
and eventually the bones of several different of big animal discoveries.

00:49:56.990 --> 00:49:59.960
They were brought here to the museum, Professor Owen...

